message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
type: software
title: "Baku bus route efficiency: measurement, travel model and fleet-neutral redesign from open data"
authors:
  - family-names: Samadov
    given-names: Ismat
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7919-4950"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Baku, Azerbaijan"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ismatsamadov/route_efficiency"
keywords:
  - public transport
  - bus network
  - network design
  - Baku
  - open data
abstract: >-
  Measures how efficiently Baku's bus routes serve riders from public data alone
  (AYNA's map, a population grid, OpenStreetMap, BakuBus boardings), builds a
  door-to-door travel model checked against observed ridership, and searches for a
  fleet-neutral redesign whose gain is checked over other trip samples and
  assumptions. Every input is committed and every result regenerates from three
  commands. The code is MIT-licensed; the data keep their own terms (see README).
